  "id": "microsaccades",
  "term": "microsaccades",
  "definition": "Microsaccades are tiny, involuntary eye movements that happen while a person is trying to keep their gaze fixed. In psychology and vision research, they are studied because they relate to visual processing and appear to track shifts in attention, including both perceptual and working-memory attention.",
